      "title": "Brian Niccol's Starbucks Turnaround Is Quietly Working -- Even With Profit Cut in Half. The July 29 Test Comes Next.",
      "summary": "Starbucks stock trades near 52-week highs despite fiscal 2025 profits being cut in half, as the market prices in CEO Brian Niccol's turnaround before it fully materializes in earnings. The recovery is driven by increasing customer traffic, with U.S. comparable sales up 7.1% and transactions up 4.3% in Q2 FY2026. However, the stock's 45x P/E ratio leaves little room for error, and the July 29 earnings report will be critical to validate whether the margin recovery continues as promised.",
